+{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdP3EHr8Ru63HPkWxfayV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015ErA46k26gVLsbjMUWgX9Q","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"delegate heavy \"Write a TypeScript module implementing Operational Transform for a collaborative text editor. Output ONLY the TypeScript code for the file src/ot.ts, no markdown fences, no commentary.\n\nThe file must import types from './models.js' exactly like this:\nimport type { Operation } from './models.js';\n\nwhere models.ts contains:\nexport interface InsertOperation { type: 'insert'; position: number; text: string; }\nexport interface DeleteOperation { type: 'delete'; position: number; count: number; }\nexport type Operation = InsertOperation | DeleteOperation;\n\nExport exactly these three functions:\n\n1. export function applyOperation(content: string, op: Operation): string\n   - insert: return content with op.text inserted at op.position\n   - delete: return content with op.count chars removed starting at op.position\n   - Treat a delete with count 0 as a no-op.\n\n2. export function transformOperation(op1: Operation, op2: Operation): Operation\n   - Returns op1 transformed as if op2 (a concurrent operation) has ALREADY been applied to the document. Returns a NEW object, never mutates inputs.\n   - insert vs insert: if op1.position < op2.position, unchanged; otherwise (>=, including ties) shift op1.position by op2.text.length.\n   - insert vs delete: if op1.position <= op2.position, unchanged; else if op1.position >= op2.position + op2.count, subtract op2.count from position; else (insert falls inside deleted range) set position to op2.position.\n   - delete vs insert: if op2.position <= op1.position, add op2.text.length to op1.position; else if op2.position >= op1.position + op1.count, unchanged; else (insert lands inside the delete range) add op2.text.length to op1.count so the range still covers through its original end.\n   - delete vs delete: compute overlap of ranges [op1.position, op1.position+op1.count) and [op2.position, op2.position+op2.count). New count = op1.count - overlapLength. New position = op1.position - min(op2.count, max(0, op1.position - op2.position)). A resulting count of 0 is fine (no-op delete).\n\n3. export function validateOperation(op: unknown, contentLength: number): op is Operation\n   - A TypeScript type-guard. Returns true only if: op is a non-null object; op.type is 'insert' or 'delete'; op.position is an integer >= 0.\n   - For insert: op.text is a string, and op.position <= contentLength.\n   - For delete: op.count is an integer >= 1, and op.position + op.count <= contentLength.\n\nConstraints: strict TypeScript (no 'any' — use type narrowing on a Record<string, unknown> cast or 'in' checks), must compile under strict mode, ESLint eslint:recommended + @typescript-eslint/recommended clean. Include brief JSDoc on each export. Double-check every branch of the transform rules against the spec above before answering.\"","description":"Delegate OT module to heavy worker","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8128,"cache_read_input_tokens":38790,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8128},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a409ebf-12f6-4e9c-acf6-ec7732f2f2cc","uuid":"f62e22c4-0a43-4611-a662-f8312a5daeec","request_id":"req_011CdP3EGFt6GUvFi3XFqYbd"}
